<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<!--
  Sample-violation fixture for the matchline BuildingSync policy ruleset
  (assets/schematron/matchline_policy-1.0.0.sch, issue #1293).

  It is a writer export (tests/test_buildingsync_policy.py::_policy_model)
  with three policy violations worked into it:

    * ML-POL-001 - the served thermal zone lost every zone-load-impacting
      input (its space floor area and its scheduled airflow), so the HVAC
      system's sizing capacity has no zone load behind it;
    * ML-POL-002 - the fan lost the LinkedSystemID that ties its airflow to
      the HVAC system whose sizing it serves;
    * ML-POL-003 - the fenestration element was renamed to a bare index, so
      its thermal value no longer names its source construction (a
      drawing-derived construction id or an ASHRAE 90.1-2019 Table 5.5
      library id).

  The document stays XSD-valid: it breaks policy, not structure.
-->
